course: dictionary
lesson: 9048
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word sleep can do different jobs in a sentence. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «Anger and excitement release adrenaline, which speeds up the heart and wakes the brain, and it takes time to calm down before sleep.» Here sleep is a noun, the rest you get at night.
explain: Sleep can also be a verb, an action you do. «In Belfast, when Roisin's friend sleeps over and whispers, "Is your house always like this?"» The words sleeps over tell you the friend stays the night. That is a sleepover, so the context clue points to the meaning.
explain: The hedgehog sentence shows sleep as resting with your eyes closed and your mind switched off. «A hedgehog curled up in a pile of leaves in winter may breathe only a few times a minute; it is not just sleeping, its whole body has slowed down to save energy.» To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Sleep is a verb (to sleep) and a noun (the state of sleeping, or how much rest you get).
fact: The verb forms are sleep, sleeps, slept and sleeping.
fact: «Go to sleep» means start sleeping, and «sleep on it» means think about something overnight before you decide.
fact: A sleepover is when a friend stays the night.
fact: Children need about 9 to 12 hours of sleep a night to stay healthy.
exercise: «Anger and excitement release adrenaline, and it takes time to calm down before sleep.» In this sentence, what does sleep mean? | *The rest you get at night | A long walk home | A small bed on a train | A sleepover with friends
exercise: «When Roisin's friend sleeps over» means the friend will: | Walk home early | *Stay the night | Go out to play | Sleep on the bus
exercise: Mia sleeps 9 hours on Monday and 11 hours on Tuesday. How many hours did she sleep in total? | 19 | 22 | 21 | *20
test: Which form is the past tense of sleep? | sleepy | *slept | sleeping | sleeps
test: Which word means a friend stays the night? | *Sleepover | Sleepy head | Sleeping bag | Sleep in
exam: Why does a hedgehog breathe only a few times a minute in winter? | *Its whole body slows down to save energy | It has a cold | It is playing a game | It is running fast
